  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>The reaction of aniline (aromatic amine) with nitrous acid results in the diazonium salt formation which is benzene diazonium chloride.When benzene diazonium chloride reacts with N, N - dimethyl aniline at ice cold condition gives p - dimethyl aminoazobenzene. It is an example of coupling reaction.</p><p><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/59b0b118-3c19-4176-9fa4-be97b865961f.png\" style=\"width: 758px; height: 206px;\" /></p>",
